### They find parenting more rewarding as the baby becomes happier and more interactive.

13 of 127 posts.

Some describe an easy baby from the start; others describe a hard beginning becoming more enjoyable with smiles, awareness, mobility and communication. Accounts span nearly two months to 14 months, including a toddler whose mood changed after walking. They share hope and things to anticipate while describing the particular care and support around them.

- "He started walking 3 weeks ago and he became a wonderful little guy. Complete change. […]" [sr077-0166]
- "That very needy and cranky baby is now 8 months and the happiest baby around. […]" [sr008-0115]
- "[…] It feels amazing after the whole newborn phase where it was really hard to bond with him. […]" [sr107-0060]
- "[…] Don’t let all these posts scare you, not every experience is like that! :)" [sr007-0024]
- "You have to work at it. I never gave up trying to make things work. But at 5 months they start to help you by just, being better at stuff." [sr036-0104]

**But:** An enjoyable stage does not remove disrupted sleep or care demands; the easy six-month-old account also explicitly describes help: "She knows I’m sleep deprived because we’re going through another sleep regression, she knows I never get to eat my food without my son either trying to steal it or crying for me to hold him." [sr027-0145] "[…] We’ve had great support with free childcare with MIL watching our baby while we’re at work and I watch her on my days off from work during weekdays." [sr046-0068]

