### They enjoy discovering the child's particular interests and preferences.

6 of 124 posts.

They enjoy the child sharing a passion, choosing books, making music or showing a familiar preference for quiet morning time. The nature outing includes boys aged four and two, two accounts describe two-year-olds, and several ages are unknown. A harmonica, Gruffalo reading and Ring of Fire become memorable family stories.

- "[…] Glad that my boys are sharing my passion for nature and wildlife. […]" [sr006-0124]
- "She figured out how to play the harmonica without help." [sr019-0157]
- "I had to read it to her 6 times.  Then she  "read" it to me a couple of times.  She was so excited to have a new Gruffalo book and a new character" [sr109-0067]
- "[…] Then he started belting out “Ring of Fire” and happily jumping in a circle. […]" [sr118-0093]

**But:** A quiet or sweet preference is not the whole temperament: "Please note though that this child is also an absolute terror who demands "hot cakes" every Saturday morning […]" [sr092-0116]

