### They weigh another child or the end of childbearing against the stage they now enjoy.

7 of 124 posts.

They want a sibling bond, feel the family is incomplete, fear restarting infancy, or grieve that more children may be impossible. The focal children include four-, nine-, ten-, 12-, 18- and almost-23-month-olds. One pair of near posts repeats the same one-and-done question and account; another describes infertility, IVF and disagreement with a partner, while another describes health limits after losses.

- "I've recently been feeling like our family isn't quite complete. This is going to sound crazy but I'd love if I could have a second who popped out as a 1-year-old." [sr049-0025]
- "[…] I’m absolutely terrified baby #2 will hit me like a brick wall. […]" [sr069-0037]
- "[…] Im excited to see them grow and learn, but im sad that I am losing my little babies. […]" [sr026-0092]
- "[…] I also love having some of my independence back." [sr080-0112]

**But:** Enjoying the current child does not settle family size or ensure both parents want another: "[…] he really only wanted a kid “for the experience” and realized he doesn’t want this experience again. […]" [sr069-0088]

