### They celebrate the child settling or sleeping with less help and hope the improvement lasts.

15 of 124 posts.

They report longer naps or night stretches, settling independently, easier transitions, or dropping a pacifier. Named ages run from two to 18 months, and some ages remain unknown. Approaches range from following cues and waiting to changing rooms, using a familiar scent, moving to a bed and Ferber check-ins; these are reported experiences rather than evidence that one approach caused the improvement.

- "I kept reading developmentally naps start to lengthen around 5-6 months and my son turned 5 months last Monday and LITERALLY that week started sleeping 1-2 hours alone." [sr012-0153]
- "Kiddo has slowly become more and more an independent sleeper without any sleep-training whatsoever. […]" [sr089-0090]
- "[…] I just have the environment ready and let her dictate her nap schedule. […]" [sr060-0064]
- "[…] First night (3/5/10 minute Ferber check-ins) he was out before the 10 minute check-in. […]" [sr120-0006]
- "[…] One thing I wasn’t expecting is that she stopped asking for her pacifier completely. […]" [sr047-0029]

**But:** Some wins are brief or emotionally mixed: "She slept for 10 minutes before getting offended though […]" [sr078-0032] "What made me emotional was realizing that the nights you do fall asleep on us are becoming numbered […]" [sr126-0066]

